# `optim::OptimaAlgorithm`

The four algorithms of `optima`.

`MeritMethod` minimises the objective plus a penalty for constraint violation, with the weight raised until the constraints hold; it is simple and robust but slow to reach tight accuracy. `SequentialQP` solves a quadratic model of the problem at each step and is the best general choice. `WorkingSet` is the same sequential approach that keeps and reuses a set of active constraints between steps, which pays off when few constraints are active. `InternalProtocol` is an interior (barrier) method: inequalities are kept strictly satisfied and a barrier parameter is driven to zero, which suits many inequalities and problems whose objective is undefined outside the feasible region.

## Fields

### `MeritMethod`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

Penalty method.

### `SequentialQP`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

Sequential quadratic programming (the default).

### `WorkingSet`

`enumerator`, default `2`.

SQP with a persistent working set.

### `InternalProtocol`

`enumerator`, default `3`.

Interior (barrier) method.

## Guidance

Set as `OptimaOptions::algorithm`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

All four on one problem; they agree on the answer.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  for (const optim::OptimaAlgorithm algorithm : {optim::OptimaAlgorithm::MeritMethod, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::SequentialQP, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::WorkingSet, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::InternalProtocol}) {
    optim::OptimaOptions options;
    options.algorithm = algorithm;
    const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
    out.writeln(optim::optima_algorithm_name(algorithm), ": x =", result.params.at("x").items<double>());
  }
}
```

### Example 2

The algorithm that ran is recorded in the state and the output record.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.algorithm = optim::OptimaAlgorithm::WorkingSet;
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("state.algorithm =", optim::optima_algorithm_name(result.algorithm), ", output.algorithm =", result.output.algorithm);
}
```

### Example 3

Cost in objective evaluations. The counts differ widely on the same problem.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  for (const optim::OptimaAlgorithm algorithm : {optim::OptimaAlgorithm::MeritMethod, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::SequentialQP, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::WorkingSet, optim::OptimaAlgorithm::InternalProtocol}) {
    optim::OptimaOptions options;
    options.algorithm = algorithm;
    const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
    out.writeln(optim::optima_algorithm_name(algorithm), ": evaluations =", result.function_evaluations);
  }
}
```

